===== 1. Existing routines in schema public (prokind f = function, p = procedure) =====
SELECT p.proname AS routine,
       CASE p.prokind WHEN 'f' THEN 'FUNCTION' WHEN 'p' THEN 'PROCEDURE' END AS kind,
       pg_get_function_result(p.oid) AS returns,
       p.prorettype = 'trigger'::regtype AS is_trigger_function,
       CASE WHEN p.prorettype = 'trigger'::regtype
            THEN 'runs only when its trigger fires'
            ELSE 'callable: SELECT * FROM ' || p.proname || '(...)' END AS how_it_runs
FROM pg_proc p
WHERE p.pronamespace = 'public'::regnamespace
ORDER BY kind, routine;
           routine            |   kind   |              returns               | is_trigger_function |               how_it_runs                
------------------------------+----------+------------------------------------+---------------------+------------------------------------------
 check_alert_event_instrument | FUNCTION | trigger                            | t                   | runs only when its trigger fires
 evaluate_price_alerts        | FUNCTION | trigger                            | t                   | runs only when its trigger fires
 ingest_tick                  | FUNCTION | TABLE(status text, tick_id bigint) | f                   | callable: SELECT * FROM ingest_tick(...)
(3 rows)

